WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.794
You're Bertha Benz.

00:00:01.804 --> 00:00:03.824
It's August 5th, 1888.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.527
Your husband Carl built this motor car.

00:00:06.537 --> 00:00:08.381
But he's a poor salesman.

00:00:08.391 --> 00:00:10.456
So without telling him, you take your

00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:13.331
two teenage sons and drive from Mannheim

00:00:13.341 --> 00:00:14.378
to Pforzheim.

00:00:14.388 --> 00:00:16.290
About 106 kilometers.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.626
No one has driven a car that

00:00:18.636 --> 00:00:19.105
far.

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:21.942
In Wiesloch, you buy fuel, a solvent

00:00:21.952 --> 00:00:24.528
called ligroin, at the town pharmacy.

00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:26.291
A fuel line clogs.

00:00:26.301 --> 00:00:28.018
You clear it with your hat pin.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.818
The brakes wear out, so a cobbler

00:00:29.828 --> 00:00:31.128
nails on leather.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.961
The first brake linings.

00:00:32.971 --> 00:00:34.821
Back home, you tell Carl:

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:36.850
add a lower gear for the hills.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.063
That pharmacy is now called the world's

00:00:39.073 --> 00:00:40.860
first filling station.
